{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he urged them greatly</b> — Lot acquired merit through his urging them, and he had good desire in bringing in guests. And they were refusing in order to bring him merit, and therefore they listened to him in the end, for at first they did not want to come to his house, for he is not a blameless righteous man. And our Sages said (Bava Metzi'a 87a): one refuses to a lesser person but one does not refuse to a great person. And if so, it would be in the manner of human courtesy:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The citation ב\"מ פז resolved as Bava Metzi'a 87a (chapter index following standard printed editions)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:22.633077272Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}